Package: zuutf
Title: Fast Unicode Validation and Transcoding with 'simdutf'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Daniel", "Lemire", role = "cph",
           comment = "simdutf, bundled in src/vendor/simdutf"),
    person("The simdutf authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "simdutf, bundled in src/vendor/simdutf"))
Description: Validates text and converts it between 'UTF-8', 'UTF-16'
    and 'UTF-32' in either byte order and 'Latin-1', counts characters,
    detects encodings, and encodes and decodes 'Base64', with a bundled
    copy of the 'simdutf' library (<https://github.com/simdutf/simdutf>).
    'simdutf' chooses single instruction, multiple data (SIMD) code for
    the running processor at first use, so validation and conversion run
    at gigabytes per second. Every validation and conversion can report
    the position of the first ill-formed sequence, in the units of the
    input. Character, raw and list-of-raw input are accepted, and invalid
    input can raise an error, be replaced with U+FFFD, or give a missing
    value. The same functions are published to other packages as a
    registered C interface.
